argus-scanner (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Map every finding that has a CWE to the OWASP Top 10.  Bundled editions
    are 2017, 2021 (default) and 2025; a CWE may belong to more than one
    category (CWE-259 is both A02:2021 and A07:2021).
  * Expose the mapping in JSON (`finding.owasp`, `summary.by_owasp`,
    `summary.owasp_version`), SARIF (`owasp/aNN-YYYY` tags and properties),
    text and Markdown (OWASP column and distribution table) and the GUI
    (finding details, summary and scan options).
  * Add `argus owasp` to browse an edition and map CWEs, plus
    `--owasp-version`, `--owasp-file` and `--no-owasp` for scan/sast/sca.
  * Ship the catalog as `argus/owasp_top10.json` and add
    `scripts/update_owasp.py`, so a new OWASP edition can be regenerated from
    the official OWASP/Top10 repository without changing the code.
  * Bump the version so the portable archive, wheel and Debian package agree.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0300

argus-scanner (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the Ubuntu ecosystem next to Debian.  Releases are addressed as
    Ubuntu:<YY.MM>[:LTS] (22.04:LTS, 24.04:LTS, 24.10), detected from
    /etc/os-release or the debian/changelog distribution and overridable with
    --deb-suite.  Ubuntu versions use the dpkg comparator and the purl
    namespace is pkg:deb/ubuntu/.
  * Accept Debian-family packages in debian/control, dpkg status
    (--deb-root/--deb-status) and binary .deb files (--deb); packages without
    a known release are skipped with a warning instead of matching another
    branch.
  * Expose the Debian/Ubuntu inputs in the GUI: system root, dpkg status file,
    .deb list and release, including directory and multi-file pickers.
  * Add Ubuntu to supported OSV ecosystems; keep the ~800 MB Ubuntu and
    ~85 MB Debian offline archives opt-in via `argus db update --ecosystem`.
  * Bump the version so the portable archive, wheel and Debian package agree.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0300

argus-scanner (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Surface Semgrep fixes as suggested replacements in JSON
    (`suggested_fix`), SARIF (`fixes[]`), Markdown, text and the GUI.
  * Add review-only fixes to the Flask debug, YAML load, Paramiko host-key,
    cookie flags and Go TLS rules; nothing is written to the sources.
  * Keep the reported severity unchanged when a fix is present and cover the
    rule structure and end-to-end behaviour with tests.
  * Bump the version so the portable archive, wheel and Debian package agree.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0300

argus-scanner (1.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Use tomli for TOML configuration files on Python 3.10 (tomllib exists
    from 3.11 only).  This fixes suppression lists and project config on
    the minimum supported interpreter.
  * Declare tomli as a conditional dependency in pyproject.toml.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0300

argus-scanner (1.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the binary package architecture independent (Architecture: all,
    about 300 kB).  The wheel set is no longer vendored: the package ships
    only the pure-Python argus wheel, and the runtime is built during
    installation, so it always matches the local architecture and Python ABI.
  * Install the latest Semgrep from PyPI when the package is configured,
    which removes the need to rebuild the package for every Semgrep release.
  * Replace argus-update-semgrep with argus-setup-runtime: it provisions,
    upgrades, pins, lists and removes the runtime, and supports offline
    installation from a wheel directory.
  * Raise the Python requirement to 3.10, matching current Semgrep releases.
  * Drop the vendored-wheel exception to Debian Policy 4.13: the source
    package no longer contains third-party binaries.
  * Remove the pip-managed Semgrep environment used by 1.1.0-2 on upgrade.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0300

argus-scanner (1.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fetch the latest Semgrep from PyPI on first installation so the rule
    engine can be updated independently of the package.  The bundled copy
    remains as a fallback; the download is best-effort and an offline
    installation still succeeds.
  * Add argus-update-semgrep to install, upgrade, pin or remove that copy,
    including offline installation from a wheel directory.
  * Depend on python3-venv for the isolated Semgrep environment.
  * Remove the pip-managed environment on purge.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0300

